Description: wayland: handle all outputs disappearing without segfaulting
 If you switch TTYs while mpv is playing, wlroots compositors will remove
 all outputs from the registry. This segfaults when you switch back since
 we try to access cleared memory. Rework this so wl->current_output is
 given null when appropriate and properly guarded. You still need at
 least one output to initially place the surface, but in general they can
 all disappear during runtime and it should work. Change the log to
 verbose because that becomes just noise in this case (switching TTYs).
 The surface entrance event happens later and should get all the proper
 parameters.
 .
 Sparky Stereo OS: carried as it is, as the base 0063 needs (row 835): it makes wl->current_output null when no known output holds the surface and guards every use of it.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/commit/3847a8157f6e44d7788dea2d1c172bc20bc50120
Author: Dudemanguy
Applied-Upstream: v0.42.0
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
